thread:
morgan: Quick design question — how should the side rail behave when users deep-link to a nested item that was regrouped last week? e.g. old /workspaces/w/1234/models -> now lives under /assets/models. Thoughts? :thinking:

tara: TL;DR: keep public deep-links stable. We should surface the new location in the UI but let old URLs resolve via aliasing. Also need a short onboarding toast on first visit.

devin: Alias table is straightforward to implement. Router can check alias map on mismatch. My worry is breadcrumbs showing old path vs new grouping — could confuse users.

alex: Product +1 to preserving URLs. UX pattern: expand the new group, show breadcrumb with the new hierarchy, and add a subtle "moved" indicator next to the item name.

sam: A11y: when auto-expanding groups for deep-linked items, ensure focus management is correct. Focus should move to the item anchor and an aria-live region should announce "Navigated to X, now under Assets > Models". Also maintain aria-current on the active link.

morgan: Good — for the scroll/focus behavior, do we prefer expand -> smooth scroll -> focus, or jump -> focus? Expand then focus sounds less jarring to me.

devin: Agree on expand -> focus. Proposed implementation snippet: 
```
const handleRoute = (path) => {
  const node = findNodeByPath(path);
  if (node.group && node.group.collapsed) node.group.expand();
  requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    node.anchor.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
    node.anchor.focus({ preventScroll: true });
  });
};
```

tara: UX copy idea for the toast (first-hit): "Moved: This item now lives in Assets > Models. We’ll keep this link working for you." CTA: "Learn more" -> migration doc. Keep toast dismissible and not shown again for that org.

alex: Also show breadcrumb fallback: "Assets > Models > MyModelName" with a small muted pill "moved from Workspaces" that has tooltip explaining the reorg. We should log clicks on the tooltip/learn-more.

devin: Routing alias suggestion: keep a single source-of-truth JSON in the infra repo, simple mapping shape. Example: 
```json
{"/workspaces/:id/models/:mid": "/assets/models/:mid"}
```
Router resolves by pattern and substitutes params. We can version the mapping file by release.

sam: A11y nit on the pill: ensure the "moved" label has sufficient contrast and is keyboard reachable. If it's interactive (tooltip/learn-more) it must be a button with aria-expanded, not just a span. Contrast target >= 4.5:1 for small text.

morgan: Plan: dev implements alias + expand/focus flow; design provides toast copy + moved-pill visuals + tooltip copy; a11y to produce acceptance criteria. I'll open a tracking PR and assign tasks.

alex: Tag me when PR is ready — I want metrics: % deep-link hits that required aliasing, and any 404s over the first 2 weeks.

deploy-bot: scheduled deploy to staging: 2024-12-05 03:00 UTC :rocket:

morgan: Thanks everyone — I'll add the prototyping notes and link mocks in the PR.

tara: Quick follow-up: for internal admin links (not public), are we ok with breaking them and surfacing a migration warning in console?

alex: Admin links are lower priority but let's provide a migration tool for org admins. No silent breaks.

devin: noted. I'll include admin-only alias toggle in the mapping file (enabled per org).

morgan: Cool. I'll update the spec with the toggle and a11y checklist. Closing thread after PR opens. :white_check_mark:
